WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.800
Step-by-step installation of REau Full

2
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:10.667
1. Download the Full edition APK from the project's Releases page and open the file to install it

3
00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:17.133
Play Protect may block the installation: that is expected on this edition, which uses Accessibility

4
00:00:17.133 --> 00:00:23.800
In the Play Store, tap your profile picture, then Play Protect and the gear, and pause app scanning

5
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:28.533
Install the APK again and, after installing, turn Play Protect back on

6
00:00:28.533 --> 00:00:34.200
2. Open REau and scroll the terms of use to the end, or tap Scroll to the end

7
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:37.200
Then tap I accept

8
00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:43.467
3. Allow location while using the app: it is only used to find the dash's Wi-Fi

9
00:00:43.467 --> 00:00:47.000
Also allow the suggested Wi-Fi networks

10
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.000
4. Tap Turn on

11
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.000
and allow notifications

12
00:00:53.000 --> 00:01:00.800
5. The first time, the server-off warning asks for Accessibility: tap Open Accessibility

13
00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:08.267
REau warns that some apps, such as banking apps, may refuse to open with Accessibility on. Tap Continue

14
00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:16.000
6. On Android 13 or newer, try to turn Accessibility on first: Restricted setting appears

15
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:22.333
In Settings, Apps, REau, in the three-dot menu, tap Allow restricted settings

16
00:01:22.333 --> 00:01:26.533
Done: now REau's Accessibility can be turned on

17
00:01:26.533 --> 00:01:33.600
7. In Accessibility, open the downloaded apps list and choose REau: Android Auto server

18
00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:39.400
On Samsung, the path is Accessibility, Installed apps, and then REau

19
00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:42.667
Turn on Use REau: Android Auto server

20
00:01:42.667 --> 00:01:47.533
and tap Allow. That is what turns the Android Auto server on by itself

21
00:01:47.533 --> 00:01:54.200
8. Android Auto developer mode: tap Open Android Auto settings

22
00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:57.600
Scroll to the bottom and tap Version ten times

23
00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:00.600
Confirm with OK

24
00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:05.333
Go back to REau and tap Try again: it turns the server on by itself

25
00:02:05.333 --> 00:02:11.800
9. The first time, tap Connect so Android lets REau join the dash's Wi-Fi

26
00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:16.600
With Android Auto active and the dash ready, REau is streaming

27
00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:21.267
10. In Permissions, tap Ask for the missing ones and allow everything

28
00:02:21.267 --> 00:02:27.800
Also tap Exclude from battery optimization, so Android does not pause REau with the screen off

29
00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:33.200
Done. Set the route in Waze and put the phone away. To finish, tap Turn off

